ENTRY            14324   20250707   20250828   20250828       1522
SUBENT        14324001   20250707   20250828   20250828       1522
BIB                 11         33
TITLE      Neutron cross-section measurements on structural
           materials at ORELA
AUTHOR     (K.H.Guber,P.E.Koehler,D.Wiarda,J.A.Harvey)
REFERENCE  (J,KPS,59,1685,2011)
           #doi:10.3938/jkps.59.1685
           (C,2008INTLAK,,(FP501),2008)  Preliminary results.
INSTITUTE  (1USAORL)
FACILITY   (LINAC,1USAORL) ORELA
DETECTOR   (GLASD,SCIN) The neutron detector was an 11.1 cm
           diameter, 1.25 cm thick 6Li-glass scintillator,
           positioned in the beam at 79.815 m from the neutron
           source. The scintillator was viewed on edge by two
           12.7 cm diameter photomultipliers that were placed
           outside the neutron beam to decrease backgrounds. For
           gamma-ray measurements, a pair of deuterated benzene
            (C6D6) detectors was used.
PART-DET   (N,G)
METHOD     (TRN,PHWT) Capture and transmission measurements for
           enriched 53Cr,48Ti and natural chromium and titanium
           were performed at ORELA. The neutron transmission and
           capture cross section were measured in the energy
           range from 10 keV to 600 keV. The transmission data
           were measured at the 79.815 m flight station. The
           neutron capture experiments were performed at the 40
           m flight station of ORELA utilizing flight paths 6
           and 7. the employed experimental technique was the
           pulse-height-weighting method.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistical errors only.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by K. Guber on June 26, 2015.
HISTORY    (20150602C) BP
           (20170625A) Addition of subentries 6, 9, 10, 12
           (20190306A) BP: Subentries 4-5 target thickness update.
           (20250706U) OS. Minor correction in REFERENCE
ENDBIB              33
